                "Structured note-taking: the agent writes progress notes, to-do lists or decision logs to a file or memory store outside the window and reads them back when needed. This is how an agent keeps track across dozens of steps or even sessions. Sub-agents: a lead agent delegates focused tasks to sub-agents that each work in their own clean context and return a condensed result, so the lead's window stays small.",
